# AI PM Portfolio

A portfolio for showcasing Product Management and AI Product Management work built from coursework, research, strategy, sprint planning, roadmap design, analytics, and AI/LLM product thinking.

## Overview
This repository is meant to serve as the base for an AI Product Manager portfolio. It gathers learning material from multiple PM and AI-related classes and workshops, including:
- product research and customer interviews
- user personas and journey mapping
- competitor teardown and market analysis
- PRD, concept notes, and roadmaps
- sprint design and agile execution
- metrics, funnel analysis, and prioritization
- pricing, GTM, and business models
- AI/LLM product strategy and responsible AI thinking

The purpose is to transform these course assets into a polished, professional portfolio that demonstrates product judgment and AI PM capability.

## Why this portfolio matters
AI PM roles increasingly need a combination of:
- customer understanding
- product strategy
- experimentation and data analysis
- AI/LLM product awareness
- business and GTM thinking
- execution and prioritization

This portfolio should present you as someone who can think beyond feature delivery and instead lead with user value, strategic clarity, and measurable outcomes.

## Recommended positioning
Use a positioning statement similar to:

"AI Product Manager with a strong foundation in user research, market analysis, metrics, product strategy, and execution. I focus on building customer-centered, data-informed AI products that create measurable business value."

